{"tool_name":"biotradis","contents":["biocontainers","galaxy","bioschemas","biotools","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"biotradis","identifiers":["doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btw022"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"A set of tools to analyse the output from tradis analyses","home_url":"https://github.com/sanger-pathogens/Bio-Tradis","keywords":["Genomics"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":3350},"biotools":{"id":"biotradis","home":"https://github.com/sanger-pathogens/Bio-Tradis","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"The Bio::TraDIS pipeline provides software utilities for the processing, mapping, and analysis of transposon insertion sequencing data. The pipeline was designed with the data from the TraDIS sequencing protocol in mind, but should work with a variety of transposon insertion sequencing protocols as long as they produce data in the expected format.","addition_date":"2022-03-16T09:25:47.599906Z","last_update_date":"2022-03-16T09:25:47.602628Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:biotradis","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Andrew J. Page"},{"name":"Gemma C. Langridge"},{"name":"Jacqueline A. Keane"},{"name":"Julian Parkhill"},{"name":"Michael A. Quail"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://sanger-pathogens.github.io/Bio-Tradis/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2403"}]}],"name":"biotradis","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw022","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2016 The Author 2015. Published by Oxford University Press.Summary: Transposon insertion sequencing is a high-throughput technique for assaying large libraries of otherwise isogenic transposon mutants providing insight into gene essentiality, gene function and genetic interactions. We previously developed the Transposon Directed Insertion Sequencing (TraDIS) protocol for this purpose, which utilizes shearing of genomic DNA followed by specific PCR amplification of transposon-containing fragments and Illumina sequencing. Here we describe an optimized high-yield library preparation and sequencing protocol for TraDIS experiments and a novel software pipeline for analysis of the resulting data. The Bio-Tradis analysis pipeline is implemented as an extensible Perl library which can either be used as is, or as a basis for the development of more advanced analysis tools. This article can serve as a general reference for the application of the TraDIS methodology. Availability and implementation: The optimized sequencing protocol is included as supplementary information. The Bio-Tradis analysis pipeline is available under a GPL license at https://github.com/sanger-pathogens/Bio-Tradis.","authors":[{"name":"Barquist L."},{"name":"Boinett C.J."},{"name":"Cain A.K."},{"name":"Cummins C."},{"name":"Keane J.A."},{"name":"Langridge G.C."},{"name":"Mayho M."},{"name":"Page A.J."},{"name":"Parkhill J."},{"name":"Quail M.A."}],"citationCount":78,"date":"2016-04-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"The TraDIS toolkit: Sequencing and analysis for dense transposon mutant libraries"},"pmcid":"PMC4896371","pmid":"26794317"}],"topic":[{"term":"Mobile genetic elements","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0798"},{"term":"Workflows","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0769"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"biotradis","home":"https://bio.tools/biotradis","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"The Bio::TraDIS pipeline provides software utilities for the processing, mapping, and analysis of transposon insertion sequencing data. The pipeline was designed with the data from the TraDIS sequencing protocol in mind, but should work with a variety of transposon insertion sequencing protocols as long as they produce data in the expected format.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"galaxy":{"version":"1.4.5","first_com